10 Legal, Ethical, Social & Professional Considerations
•	GDPR compliance: no personal or real company data collected (BCS 2023).
•	Responsible disclosure: no offensive security testing.
•	Confidentiality: all evaluation data simulated.
•	Professional ethics: adheres to the BCS Code of Conduct (BCS 2023).
•	Social impact: enhances SME cyber resilience and awareness.
________________________________________
11 Expected Outcomes
•	A documented and tested Cyber Essentials Readiness Toolkit.
•	A prototype dashboard visualising compliance progress.
•	A professional artefact suitable for consultancy use.
•	Demonstrated mastery of cybersecurity governance and project-management techniques (Dawson 2015).
